    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Binary search</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Search on the slope</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/find-peak-element/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 162</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Find Peak Element</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Binary search works without sorting: compare mid with mid + 1 and walk uphill. Because the edges count as minus infinity, every uphill walk must end at a peak, so the uphill half always holds one. O(log n) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
  },
